#: ../../usage.rst:2
msgid "How to Use the Solar Flare Alert"
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:5
msgid "Assembling the Device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:7
msgid "Here are all the components of the device:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:8
msgid "Wire ring inserted in socket strip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:13
msgid "1. Insert the wire ring in the center of the socket strip and insert the LED into the ping-pong ball."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:16
msgid "LED placed inside ping-pong ball"
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:21
msgid "Plug the cables into the outer plugs of the socket strip. Ensure the **black cable is on the left side** when viewed from the perspective of the ESP32."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:24
msgid "Cables correctly inserted in socket strip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:29
msgid "Make sure the black cable goes to the left side, marked with a black marker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:31
msgid "USB cable plugged in"
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:36
msgid "Plug in the USB cable to power the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:38
msgid "Fully assembled Solar Flare Alert device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:43
msgid "Your solar flare alert is now physically assembled and ready to connect to the WiFi."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:46
msgid "Connecting to the WiFi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:48
msgid "Power on the solar flare alert. The LED will start blinking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:50
msgid "If the blinking **stops after a few seconds**, the device successfully connected to a known WiFi network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:52
msgid "If it **keeps blinking**, open the WiFi settings on your phone or computer and connect to the access point named **WifiManager**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:54
msgid "The phone should show a sign-in page. If it does not, open a web browser on the phone and type ``http://192.168.4.1`` in the address field. Stay on **WifiManager** while that page loads. If it still does not open, turn mobile data off and try again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:60
msgid "Earlier lamps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:63
msgid "Lamps sold before this setup page was updated do not show a sign-in window. The phone can be connected to the lamp while the browser still cannot open the page. Try the following once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:65
msgid "Watch the LED. If it **stops blinking**, the lamp has already joined a saved network. Reconnect your phone to your home Wi-Fi. Nothing else is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:67
msgid "If the LED **keeps blinking**, join the Wi-Fi network **WifiManager**. It is an open network and has no password."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:69
msgid "Turn mobile data off, and stay on **WifiManager** when the phone says the network has no internet. Otherwise the phone sends the address through the mobile network, and the lamp never sees it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:71
msgid "On the phone, open a web browser and type ``http://192.168.4.1`` in the address field. Keep the ``http://``. Typing the number into a search box does not reach the lamp."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:73
msgid "If the page does not load, turn the lamp off, wait ten seconds, turn it on, and repeat from step 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:75
msgid "If the page is still blank, stop retrying. On these lamps the setup program accepts the Wi-Fi connection and then does not answer, whether the browser is on a phone or a computer. The lamp needs the updated setup program (``wifi_manager.py``) before it can be joined to a new network. A network it has already saved keeps working."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:56
msgid "Choose your home WiFi network from the list and enter the password."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage.rst:58
msgid "You're done! Reconnect your device to your normal WiFi. The solar flare alert will now show the Sun's activity level."
msgstr ""
